#: ../../source/guides/devops/suites-and-verdicts.rst:53
msgid ""
"Every row carries the command that runs it, and every message about a "
"suite quotes it. A verdict that says something is stale without saying "
"how to un-stale it is a verdict people route around."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/suites-and-verdicts.rst:56
msgid ""
"**Every row is a** ``make`` **target, in whichever repository the suite "
"belongs to.** The alternative is quoting the selection itself — "
"``freeports-dev test -- -m 'not integration_tests'`` — in the hook, in "
"this table and in the repository's own documentation, which is three "
"copies of one decision, and the failure mode of three copies is that a "
"fourth reader invents a fifth. The selection has one spelling, ``--fast``"
" / ``--slow``, in the command that owns it, and the target is what a "
"message quotes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/suites-and-verdicts.rst:64
msgid "Why a suite is recorded rather than announced"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/suites-and-verdicts.rst:66
msgid ""
"An outcome passed on a command line — ``ci-check --suite fast:passed`` — "
"says what has just happened, and it is **silent about everything that has"
" not**. A gate that runs two of six suites and reports \"tests: ok\" is "
"worse than one that reports nothing, because a reader believes it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/suites-and-verdicts.rst:70
msgid "So each suite writes ``reports/suite-<name>.json``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/suites-and-verdicts.rst:76
msgid ""
"and ``ci-check`` reads the lot. The commit is the point of the file. "
"Without it there is no telling a suite that passed on this code from one "
"that passed a fortnight ago, and the fast/slow split would quietly become"
" a way of never running the slow half."
msgstr ""

